#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:2
msgid "Decommissioning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:4
msgid "Snapd runs on three system types:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:6
msgid "[Ubuntu Core]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:7
msgid "Hybrid Classic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:8
msgid "Classic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:10
msgid ""
"The approach to decommissioning snapd differs depending on the system type, "
"as snapd provides core system functionality on Ubuntu Core and Hybrid "
"Classic systems, but is an optional package on Classic Ubuntu systems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:14
msgid "Ubuntu Core systems"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:16
msgid ""
"On Ubuntu Core systems, snapd is a fundamental component of the operating "
"system and part of the overall device image and product lifecycle. Ubuntu "
"Core devices are typically deployed as integrated IoT or appliance-style "
"systems with a fixed software lifetime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:18
msgid ""
"Decommissioning of Ubuntu Core systems should be performed at the system "
"level rather than by removing snapd, and is therefore outside the scope of "
"this section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:20
msgid "Hybrid Classic systems"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:22
msgid ""
"Hybrid Classic system is a classic system with kernel snap e.g. Ubuntu 26.04 "
"using the TPM backed FDE installation option. It provides a Classic Ubuntu "
"user experience but relies on snapd for essential system functionality such "
"as system snaps, recovery, and full disk encryption. On these systems, snapd "
"is not an optional component and should not be removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:24
msgid ""
"Decommissioning of Hybrid Classic systems should be performed at the system "
"level rather than by removing snapd, and is therefore outside the scope of "
"this section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:26
msgid "Classic systems"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:28
msgid ""
"On Classic Ubuntu systems, snapd is an optional component and may be "
"decommissioned if it is no longer required. Snapd is bootstrapped by the "
"snapd deb package, but installation of any non-essential snap (core, gadget, "
"kernel, snapd) would also trigger installation of snapd snap. On Classic "
"Ubuntu systems, re-execution is enabled by default, which means the deb "
"package will re-execute to snapd provided by the snap package whenever that "
"version is more recent than the deb package version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:30
msgid "Decommissioning snapd on Classic systems involves:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:32
#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:47
msgid "Removing installed snaps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:33
msgid "Removing the snapd package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:34
msgid ""
"Removing remaining snap data, state directories, and stored snapshots "
"(including user, system, and configuration data)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:36
msgid "Typical locations where snap data may remain include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:38
msgid "`/var/snap/`:         Snap system data and persistent application data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:39
msgid ""
"`/var/lib/snapd/`:    Snapd state, installed snap revisions, assertions, "
"snapshots"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:40
msgid "`/var/cache/snapd/`:  Downloaded snap packages and cache"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:41
msgid ""
"`/snap/`:             Mounted snap squashfs files (read-only runtime files)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:42
msgid "`/home/$USER/snap/`:  Per-user snap data, configuration, and user files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:43
msgid "`/home/$USER/.snap/`: Authentication data and signing keys"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:44
msgid "`/var/log/journal/`:  Persistent logging (configurable)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:45
msgid "`/run/log/journal/`:  Non-persistent logging (default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:49
msgid ""
"Removal of the snapd snap requires first removing all other snaps. Removing "
"installed snaps with `snap remove --purge <snap>` prevents taking an "
"automatic snapshot, however existing {ref}`snapshots <how-to-guides-manage-"
"snaps-create-data-snapshots>` still remain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:51
msgid "Removing the snapd snap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:53
msgid ""
"When all other snaps have been removed the snapd snap can also be removed. "
"Removal of the snapd snap does not remove /var/lib/ in order to allow the "
"snapd deb package to function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:56
msgid "Removing the snapd deb package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:58
msgid ""
"Removal of the snapd deb package with `sudo apt remove --purge snapd` "
"removes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:59
msgid "`/var/snap`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:60
msgid "`/var/lib/snapd/`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:61
msgid "`/var/cache/snapd/`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:62
msgid "`/snap/`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:64
msgid "User data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:66
msgid ""
"If required, root and other user data should be manually removed by wiping `/"
"root/snap/` and `/root/.snap/` as well as `/home/$USER/snap/` and `/home/"
"$USER/.snap/`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:68
msgid "Removing journal logs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/decommissioning.md:70
msgid ""
"If deemed necessary, journal containing snapd logs can be removed, but this "
"cannot be done cleanly without impacting non-snapd logging. Identify if the "
"journal contains any snapd files using `journalctl --directory=/var/log/"
"journal -u snapd` and remove the log if required."
msgstr ""
